<title>LITHUANIA: DANISH ODENSE BUYS 43 PCT OF BALTIJA SHIPYARD.</title>
<headline>DANISH ODENSE BUYS 43 PCT OF BALTIJA SHIPYARD.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Odense Staalskibsvaerst has bought a 43.65 percent stake in Lithuania's Baltija Shipyard in the western port town of Klaipeda for 15.02 million litas, newspaper Respublika said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The Danish firm bought the shares via the stock market in bloc trades on Tuesday, the newspaper added.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted its sources as saying the Danish company intends to invest around $10 million into Baltija and wants to take part in the sale privatisation of other companies in Lithuania, the newspaper added.</p>
<p>Baltija Shipyard had a net profit of around five million litas in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Andrius Vilkancas, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
